# HalalFlicks vet batches — no repeats across chats

**When** the owner is doing **HalalFlicks / Halalflicks movie or TV vet batches** (ok / reject / parent discretion / park / idk):

## Before offering any new batch

1. **Read** `halalflicks/config/vet_shown.json` — every title already shown in a vet batch.
2. **Read** `halalflicks/config/parked.json` — owner-parked (including idk treated as park).
3. **Read** `halalflicks/config/hand_vetted.json` — already decided titles.
4. **Do not** put any of those titles in a new batch unless the owner **explicitly** asks (e.g. “unpark DuckTales”, “ask me about Shrek again”).

## After each batch is shown

Append every offered title to `halalflicks/config/vet_shown.json` **in the same turn** (even if unanswered yet). Update `parked.json` when they say park/idk. Update `hand_vetted.json` + `rec_catalog.json` for ok/reject/discretion.

**Before ending the chat:** ask the owner to **commit** the HalalFlicks config JSON (and related rule/roadmap edits) so the next unrelated agent does not get a +changes chip.

## Batch shape (owner process)

- Mixed batches: **10 films + 10 series**, newest first; newer releases jump the queue.
- One clean numbered list only — no draft/rewrite duplicates in the same reply.
- Catalog rules: holiday-centered reject; The Rock never recommend; Harry Potter series reject (author); **R / TV-MA never recommend**; slice-of-life kids TV may have Christian-holiday episodes (flag).

## Why this exists

Chat memory alone re-offered titles across conversations. These JSON files are the durable source of truth.
